@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Activities
+
+Activities are the account activity events shown in the timeline, such as cards being created, assigned, moved, or commented on.
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities.json`
+
+Returns activity for boards the current user can access, newest activity first.
+
+Clients can filter activity by `creator_ids` and `board_ids`:
+
+```
+GET /:account_slug/activities.json?creator_ids[]=user-id&board_ids[]=board-id
+```
+
+__Response:__
+
+```json
+[
+  {
+    "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
+    "action": "card_published",
+    "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+    "description": "David added \"The logo isn't big enough\"",
+    "particulars": {},
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/1",
+    "eventable_type": "Card",
+    "eventable": {
+      "id": "03f5v9zo9qlcwwpyc0ascnikz",
+      "number": 1,
+      "title": "The logo isn't big enough"
+    },
+    "board": {
+      "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcm",
+      "name": "Fizzy"
+    },
+    "creator": {
+      "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
+      "name": "David"
+    }
+  }
+]
+```
+
+The `eventable`, `board`, and `creator` objects use the same representations as the corresponding API endpoints. The `particulars` object contains event-specific details: `assignee_ids` for assignment changes, `old_board` and `new_board` for board changes, `old_title` and `new_title` for title changes, and `column` for triage events. Other events return an empty `particulars` object.
